<title>UK: Smith talk highlights retail bid hopes.</title>
<headline>Smith talk highlights retail bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Growing expectations of a major takeover bid in the UK retail sector were highlighted on Monday by reports that chemists chain Boots Plc had considered a bid for WH Smith Group Plc, analysts said.</p>
<p>Boots said in a statement it had looked at Smiths earlier this year, but had decided instead to concentrate on international expansion and developing its core business.</p>
<p>Smith's shares were up 4 pence at 424 pence in late morning trade, while Boots were 6 pence higher at 603 pence. Traders said the gains were part of a general recovery by retail stocks after Friday's jitters over the strength of pre-Christmas sales.</p>
</text>
